o, that's the Fireman.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, I'm talking about the blue book. Are you talking about the regular hardcover?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T17:34:23-07:00","id":852140,"title":"","content":"It's a gold-on-blue version of the image of the Fireman at the point he Erupted. <a href=\"http://i.ebayimg.com/00/s/MTIwMFgxNjAw/z/FHgAAOSwPhdVJfPk/$_57.JPG\" target=\"_blank\">A bigger picture</a> on eBay.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":221,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","user":"Craig Oxbrow","date":". 03-23-2016, 08:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T18:42:38-07:00","id":852165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Craig Oxbrow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/851737-the-actual-books?p=852140#post852140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a gold-on-blue version of the image of the Fireman at the point he Erupted. <a href=\"http://i.ebayimg.com/00/s/MTIwMFgxNjAw/z/FHgAAOSwPhdVJfPk/$_57.JPG\" target=\"_blank\">A bigger picture</a> on eBay.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, I would never have been able to see that from that tiny picture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T21:08:54-07:00","id":852225,"title":"","content":"Is there still any remaining possibility for digital versions of the books, with computer animations and the like, that Rich Thomas fantasized about at Gen Con all those years ago?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/140-samcwic","name":"samcwic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T22:02:34-07:00","id":852800,"title":"","content":"Yeah; for TC: \u00c6on, at least, I'd much rather have a \u201cDeluxe Digital\u201d than a deluxe physical book. I'm not so sure about TC core, Aberrant, or Adventure!, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T07:18:23-07:00","id":852954,"title":"","content":"The small-sized books were okay for the &quot;gimmicky&quot; decade that was the 90s (just think about all that comics crap), but for today I want nice, normal-sized hardcover books. With full color illustrations, please.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8890-nullapostle","name":"NullApostle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T09:29:01-07:00","id":853020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NullApostle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/851737-the-actual-books?p=852954#post852954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The small-sized books were okay for the &quot;gimmicky&quot; decade that was the 90s (just think about all that comics crap), but for today I want nice, normal-sized hardcover books. With full color illustrations, please.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I can't deny the utter awesomeness that is the 20th Anniversary Mage: The Ascension book that is getting delivered this week. I wish I had the $$$ to be in on that one. But, I think hardbacks done with that level of detail and in the size of the original books would be great. The smaller size stands out on a bookshelf and at the table. Yes, they are graphic novel sized but that's fine by me. I wouldn't mind a standard edition of the TC Core Rules and then have the era books be ultra / Deluxe / special editions. I can see the Aeon Trinity logo in all its holographic glory or Divas Mal in 3D ready to leap off the cover of the Aberrant Era source book. I'm all in on these books. I've been saving since they announced the new edition. <br /> <br /> I do like the idea of the special edition digital edition but I have no idea how that would be accomplished.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=485\" data-tempid=\"temp_485_1538393298974_786\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1277-karpomatic","name":"karpomatic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1277_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T11:28:38-07:00","id":853077,"title":"","content":"I guess if it's handled well I wouldn't mind &quot;graphic novel&quot; sized books. I wonder how those will look in PDF?<br /> I liked the format they used for <i>Adventure! - </i>it's the only book I still leaf through occasionaly. <br /> <br /> About the other stuff, I don't really care about the &quot;super-deluxe/prestige/gold-rimmed/etc.&quot; editions. IF I back the kickstarters, I'll most likely back at the level that nets me a simple hardcover volume - I can't really afford more. Beginning in May, the little money I have left over every month is pretty much commited to <i>Stellaris </i>for the foreseeable future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8890-nullapostle","name":"NullApostle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T15:34:43-07:00","id":853194,"title":"","content":"A special digital edition for Aeon might be nice, but my first concern should be ease of use to table. One of the reasons I still prefer dead tree is I find them easier to read, carry, search and reference than any electronic format. A tricked out version for Aeon specifically would be nice as a stretch goal, but table meat has to take precedence to shelf candy.<br /> <br /> Size isn't an issue so long as we can get page count. I'm not even sure I need hardback...my softcover Trinity books have held up pretty well, really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T21:47:30-07:00","id":853328,"title":"","content":"I like the Deluxe editions that I have gotten I don't need the bells and whistles but I appreciate them.<br /> Premier is fine. While the original size is fine I for one would rather have full size for the simple fact this could and hope it will be a massive book and an off size will increase page count.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T07:53:36-07:00","id":854029,"title":"","content":"Honestly I don't think we will be talking about massive books, if most of the baseline details are split in two separate books (Trinity Core and Aeon).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T04:56:16-07:00","id":854416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/851737-the-actual-books?p=854029#post854029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly I don't think we will be talking about massive books, if most of the baseline details are split in two separate books (Trinity Core and Aeon).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Agreed. If we were talking about one book for everything then it would be super thick but since there will be a core rule book and separate setting books I think the smaller size would be great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=485\" data-tempid=\"temp_485_1538393298974_786\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1277-karpomatic","name":"karpomatic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1277_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T21:09:00-07:00","id":857462,"title":"","content":"I don't care if it's Deluxe or Prestige of whatever, I just want it to be a regular, standard, hardcover RPG book :P<br /> <br /> The one objection I always had to the old ones was the nonstandard design of the things. It was a cute experiment I guess, but I'd have been much happier if they'd been laid out and printed like normal White Wolf books. Hopefully they'll be done up like normal OPP books.<br /> <br /> No gimmicks! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Comic Book companies still haven't learned that lesson.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T09:07:59-07:00","id":864331,"title":"","content":"The old books do have their own character sure, but some just didn't work out well in the end. The hardback Trinity book with the coiled spine starts to fall apart on heavy use, the plastic limited edition looks great but is a pain to use at the table. The smaller size of the softcovers make for easy enough reading, but are not that great for quick reference (can't lay them open on a table) - also, some of the spines on a percentage of the Order books were......not great. <br /> <br /> So yep, standard sized books would be my preference. <br /> <br /> Don't really have a preference on PDF's as I tend not to use them at the table. They're nice to have as a backup I guess. I'm unlikely to pay more for a 'premium' PDF / digital version unless there's something about the experience that makes it a must-have, something that the dead-tree versions can't do. I'm not suggesting PDF only content incidentally (which would frustrate me).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}